Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.25,0:00:02.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,This is the planet in 2003.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.55,0:00:05.56,Cap,,0,0,0,,And this is 2026.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.85,0:00:06.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,Both at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.90,0:00:09.48,Cap,,0,0,0,,That gap is 23 years of methane.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.10,0:00:11.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,This is Terra Vox.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.16,0:00:14.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,It turns real NASA satellite data into sound, so anyone,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.47,0:00:18.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,even without seeing a chart, can hear how Earth is changing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.52,0:00:24.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,Across every year, our values match NOAA: r = 0.992 for methane,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.04,0:00:26.11,Cap,,0,0,0,,r = 0.997 for sea level.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.51,0:00:29.31,Big,,0,0,0,,TERRA VOX
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.51,0:00:29.31,Mid,,0,0,0,,Hear how the planet changed\NNASA Space Apps Challenge 2026
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.51,0:00:29.31,Small,,0,0,0,,demondarkness010-web.github.io/terra-vox\NData: NASA GIBS and NASA SVS Earth Information Center. Checked against NOAA.\NNarration: AI voice (ElevenLabs). Not endorsed by NASA or NOAA.
